    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0162",
      "sequence": 174,
      "meaning": "The pretender says he therefore remains hidden, having no purpose apart from Hari: the Lord knows everything without being told, so why court the world for supernatural powers? Since the king is pure, wise and dear, and trusts him, concealment would now bring him terrible blame. The more detached the pretender sounds, the more the king believes him; once he sees the king’s deed, mind and speech under control, the crane-like schemer gives his name as Ekatanū. Asked respectfully to explain it, he claims he was born at the primal creation and has never taken another body, hence ‘One Body.’",
