    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0163",
      "sequence": 175,
      "meaning": "The false ascetic tells the king not to be amazed, for nothing is hard through austerity: by its power Brahmā creates, Viṣṇu protects and Śiva destroys, and nothing in the world lies beyond it. Enchanted, the king listens as the pretender relates ancient tales, analyzes action, dharma, dispassion and discernment, and describes countless marvels of creation, preservation and dissolution. Completely under his spell, Pratāpabhānu finally gives his own name. The ascetic claims he already knows the king, praises the concealment, and says rulers wisely avoid disclosing their identity—but his own great love has recognized the king’s prudence.",
