    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0165",
      "sequence": 177,
      "meaning": "The ascetic says it shall be so, but one obstacle remains: even Time will bow at the king’s feet except for the Brahmin lineage. Brahmins are always mighty through austerity, and no one can protect against their anger. If the king brings all Brahmins under his control, even Brahmā, Viṣṇu and Śiva will be subject to him; one cannot prevail against Brahmins, and only their curse can destroy him. The delighted king believes his destruction is now impossible and thanks the gracious sage for everlasting welfare. The pretender agrees, then warns the king not to blame him if his identity is forgotten when they meet again.",
